# Prices that moved, in any town (Docs/Design/30-towns-and-talk.md): herbs and meals going up or down, as the market,
# the hearth, the sickroom and the street feel it. Blanks: {item} ("herbs" or "a meal") and {price}.
# Alternatives run in parallel: the second reply answers the second remark.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Herbs dearer

scene em_herbs_up_sickbed
when topic=prices item=herbs dir=up
a : My pup's coughing and herbs are {price} a bundle. | {price} for feverfew. I counted it out twice. | The herb seller wants {price} now. For weeds.
b : Have you tried the chapel? They keep a little by. | You counted right, sadly. | Weeds that cure you aren't weeds.
a : I'll try them tomorrow. | I wish I hadn't. | Fine. Expensive weeds.
b?[healer] : Bring the pup to me. I'll stretch what I have.
b?[old] : Honey and steam. Cost me nothing when I was small.

scene em_herbs_up_hoarders
when topic=prices item=herbs dir=up place=market|street
a : Somebody's buying up all the herbs. Mark me. | Every stall's sold out of mint by noon. | {price} a bundle, and half of it stems.
b : Who'd hoard herbs? | Noon? It was gone by dawn yesterday. | Stems and a smell of mint.
a : Someone with a cellar and no shame. | Then I'll come at dawn. | That's all you get for {price}.
b?[merchant] : I sell what I'm given at what I'm charged.
b?[guard] : If someone's hoarding, the Watch would want a name.

scene em_herbs_up_cook_grumble
when topic=prices item=herbs dir=up a.job=cook|innkeeper|baker
a : My stew wants thyme and my purse says no. | {price} for a fistful of sage. I'll season with salt and prayers. | Gave the soup a sniff of rosemary. A sniff is all it gets now.
b : Nobody will notice. | Salt's cheaper. Pray harder. | A sniff's more than I get at home.
a : Everyone will notice. | I am praying. | Come eat here, then.

scene em_herbs_up_pup_question
when topic=prices item=herbs dir=up
a : Have you seen the herb stall today? | Herbs again. {price}. | I'm going to start growing my own on the sill.
b : I walked past fast with my ears down. | Again and again. | On that sill? It gets no sun.
a : It's a shame. | And we keep paying. | Then I'll grow mould.

scene em_herbs_up_forager
when topic=prices item=herbs dir=up season=spring|summer
a : At {price} a bundle I'm off to the hedges tomorrow. | The ditches are full of nettle and nobody's picking. | Why pay {price} when the hill's covered in yarrow?
b : Mind the wasps. | Nettles? Gloves, then. | Because half of it's hemlock.
a : I'll mind them. | I've got thick paws. | I know the difference. Mostly.
b?[farmer] : Mind whose hedges. I know where my sorrel grows.
b?[healer] : Bring me what you find before you eat it. Half that hill is poison.

scene em_herbs_up_winter
when topic=prices item=herbs dir=up season=autumn|winter
a : Nothing grows in this cold and the sellers know it. | Dried herbs at {price}. Dust, mostly. | Winter herbs cost twice what summer ones did.
b : Can't blame the frost for being greedy. | Dust with a good smell. | And taste half as much.
a : I can blame the seller. | That's the trouble. | Winter's a thief.
b?[merchant] : Drying takes time and space. That's in the price.

scene em_herbs_up_priest
when topic=prices item=herbs dir=up
weight 0.7
a : Can't afford herbs at {price}. Might ask the chapel. | The chapel still gives herbs to the poor, doesn't it? | I left a bundle at the chapel last month. Wish I had it back.
b : They'll help if they can. | When they have any. | Ha. No you don't.
a : I'll go tonight. | Then I'd better be quick. | Maybe a little.
b?[priest] : Take what you need. The Bright One counts what's given, not what's kept.

scene em_herbs_up_rivals
when topic=prices item=herbs dir=up band=rivals
a : I suppose you're pleased, with herbs at {price}. | Your cousin sells herbs, doesn't he? Funny how they've gone up. | You bought the last of the mint. I saw you.
b : Why would I be pleased? | Say that again and see. | I was first in line. That's all.
a : You always land on your paws. | I'll say it twice. | First in line, last to share.

scene em_herbs_up_friends_share
when topic=prices item=herbs dir=up band=friends
a : Herbs at {price}. I'm going without. | Can't buy chamomile for my bad nights now. | My poultice jar's empty and herbs cost {price}.
b : No you're not. I've a bundle hung by my door. | I'll bring you a pinch tonight. | I'll make you one. I've comfrey drying.
a : You're a good friend. | You don't have to. | I'll owe you a supper.

scene em_herbs_up_old_remedies
when topic=prices item=herbs dir=up a.stage=old
a : When I was a pup we chewed willow bark and got on with it. | Herbs at {price}. My mother would have laughed. | In my day nobody sold herbs. You knew where to look.
b : Willow bark tastes like a fence. | She'd have laughed and then cried. | Nobody knows where to look any more.
a : That's how you know it works. | She did both often. | That's what I keep saying.
b?[child] : Does willow bark taste bad?

scene em_herbs_up_brewer
when topic=prices item=herbs dir=up a.job=brewer|innkeeper
a : Hops and herbs both up. My ale's going to taste of water. | Spiced cider costs me {price} more a barrel to make. | I'll be brewing plain ale till herbs come down.
b : It already tastes of water. | Then charge more for it. | Plain ale's fine by me.
a : Watch your tongue or drink elsewhere. | And then hear about it all night. | It would be.

scene em_herbs_up_soldier
when topic=prices item=herbs dir=up a.job=guard|soldier
a : The barracks surgeon is rationing salve. | Wound herbs at {price}. Try not to get stabbed this month. | We used to get a herb ration. Not since the price went up.
b : Rationing? Be careful, then. | I'll try my hardest. | Complain to your captain.
a : I'm always careful. | Tell the robbers that. | My captain says complain to the herb seller.

scene em_herbs_up_brief
when topic=prices item=herbs dir=up
weight 0.6
a : Herbs. {price}. | Did you buy herbs today? | {price}, if you're wondering about herbs.
b : I know. | No. Not at that price. | I wasn't. Now I'm sad.
a : I know you know. | Nor me. | Sorry.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Herbs cheaper

scene em_herbs_down_glut
when topic=prices item=herbs dir=down
a : Herb stall's practically giving them away. {price} a bundle. | There's a glut of herbs. Someone's cellar must have burst. | I bought three bundles at {price}. Couldn't help myself.
b : Giving them away? I'll go now. | A cellar full of mint. Imagine the smell. | Three? What will you do with three?
a : Go quick, before the cooks get there. | Like a sweet shop. | Hang them everywhere.
b?[healer] : Good. I'll stock the shelves while I can.
b?[merchant] : Cheap now. Not for long. Buy while you're able.

scene em_herbs_down_cook_glad
when topic=prices item=herbs dir=down a.job=cook|innkeeper|baker
a : Herbs at {price}. Everything gets thyme this week. | Sage in the bread, sage in the stew, sage on the floor. | Finally my kitchen smells like a kitchen.
b : I'll come for supper. | Not on the floor, I hope. | It smelled like boiled boots before.
a : Bring coin. | Strewn sage keeps the fleas off. | It did. Hush.

scene em_herbs_down_suspicious
when topic=prices item=herbs dir=down
a : Herbs at {price}? That's suspicious. | Why are herbs so cheap? Somebody's selling bad ones. | Cheap herbs. I'd smell them before you buy.
b : Or maybe it was a good season. | Or maybe they've too many. | My nose is better than yours.
a : Never trust a good season. | Maybe. | We'll see.
b?[healer] : Sniff for mould and look for grey leaves. If it's sound, it's sound.

scene em_herbs_down_seller_sad
when topic=prices item=herbs dir=down a.role=merchant
a : I sold a whole day's herbs and made less than last week. | {price} a bundle and still they haggle. | If herbs go any lower I'll be eating them.
b : Good for us, though. | They'll haggle at nothing. | They're good for you.
a : Not for me. | They would. | Not as a whole meal.

scene em_herbs_down_child
when topic=prices item=herbs dir=down
a : Herbs are cheap. I filled the pantry. | I made a pillow of lavender, they were so cheap. | Herbs for {price}. My hearth smells sweet.
b : Lucky you. | A pillow? Do you sleep better? | Mine smells of smoke.
a : For once. | Like a stone. | Come and sit by mine.

scene em_herbs_down_old
when topic=prices item=herbs dir=down b.stage=old
a : Herbs are cheaper, grandfather. You could get your knee salve. | {price} a bundle. Shall I fetch you some? | They're selling herbs cheap at the stalls.
b : Maybe I will. The knee's been barking at me. | Fetch two. And don't let them cheat you. | Cheap is cheap. It won't last.
a : I'll go tomorrow. | They won't. | Then buy now.

scene em_herbs_down_brief
when topic=prices item=herbs dir=down
weight 0.6
a : Herbs are down. | {price} for herbs now. Not bad. | Cheap herbs this week.
b : About time. | Not bad at all. | Good to hear.
a : About time indeed. | Better than last week. | Isn't it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Meals dearer

scene em_meal_up_tavern_slate
when topic=prices item=meal dir=up place=tavern|street|market
a : The slate by the door says {price} for stew now. | A bowl of broth for {price}. It was half that last season. | I saw the new prices on the board and walked straight out.
b : Stew's still stew. | Last season was kinder. | Where did you eat, then?
a : Stew at {price} had better have meat in it. | Everything was kinder. | Nowhere. I'm hungry.
b?[innkeeper] : The grain cart charges me double. Shall I cook air?
b?[old] : Charged me {price} for gristle and a bread heel.

scene em_meal_up_family_supper
when topic=prices item=meal dir=up band=family|spouses
a : We'll be eating barley again tonight. | Food's so dear I'm watering the soup. | The pups ate everything. I've had nothing.
b : Barley again is fine by me. | I noticed. I didn't say. | Here, take my bread.
a : You always say that. | Thank you for not saying. | No, you eat it.

scene em_meal_up_laborer
when topic=prices item=meal dir=up a.job=laborer|miner|carter|woodcutter
a : I can't haul all day on a crust and a pickle. | A meal costs {price}, and they pay us the same as last year. | Lunch was water and a turnip.
b : Ask for more pay. | Same pay, more cost. Always the way. | A whole turnip?
a : And lose the work? | Always. | Half of one.

scene em_meal_up_beggar
when topic=prices item=meal dir=up a.job=beggar|servant
a : Nobody spares a bite when food's this dear. | Used to get scraps at the back door. Not now. | Folk walk faster past me when bread goes up.
b : Here. It's not much. | Times are hard for all of us. | I'm sorry.
a : Bright One keep you. | Harder for some. | So am I.

scene em_meal_up_pups
when topic=prices item=meal dir=up
a : Supper's smaller in every house this week. | The pups ask for more and I've nothing to give them. | Dear food makes everyone short-tempered.
b : They'll remember it as a lean week. | Give them mine. | Everyone's snapping at everyone.
a : I hope it's only a week. | Then you'll be hungry. | My ears are flat all day.
b?[child] : I'm hungry too.

scene em_meal_up_merchant_defends
when topic=prices item=meal dir=up b.role=merchant
a : {price} for a meal? Is it served on silver? | You've put your prices up. | Your pies have shrunk.
b : Served on wood, with my apologies. | Everyone has. The roads aren't safe. | The pies are the same. Your eyes are hungrier.
a : Then the wood is very expensive. | The roads are an excuse. | My eyes know a pie.

scene em_meal_up_cooking_home
when topic=prices item=meal dir=up
a : I'm cooking at home every night now. | No more suppers out at {price} a bowl. | I've learned to make soup from almost nothing.
b : Your cooking or {price}? Hard choice. | I miss the noise of the tavern, though. | Almost nothing is my favourite flavour.
a : Rude. | So do I. | You'd eat it and like it.

scene em_meal_up_soldier
when topic=prices item=meal dir=up a.job=guard|soldier
a : Barracks rations shrank again. | The quartermaster's cutting the bread thinner. | I could eat my own boots after a watch on this ration.
b : Thinner than it was? | Bread you can see through. | Boots are leather. Very filling.
a : Much thinner. | Like a window. | Don't tempt me.

scene em_meal_up_spring_lean
when topic=prices item=meal dir=up season=spring
a : Spring's always lean. The old stores are gone and nothing new is in. | Last year's grain is running out. | The hungry season, my mother called it.
b : Not long now till the fields come in. | And this year's isn't in. | She knew.
a : Not soon enough. | Exactly. | She did.
b?[farmer] : Wait till the first harvest. Be patient.

scene em_meal_up_winter
when topic=prices item=meal dir=up season=winter
a : Snow on the road means no carts and dear bread. | Everything's dearer when the cold sets in. | I'm burning my coin on food and firewood both.
b : Every winter the same. | Cold makes everyone a merchant. | At least you're warm and fed.
a : And every winter I forget. | And greedy. | Barely either.

scene em_meal_up_rivals
when topic=prices item=meal dir=up band=rivals
a : I hear you put your rates up too, with food so dear. | Your table still looks full. Must be nice. | You'll be fine. You always are.
b : Everyone's raised them. Don't single me out. | Mind your own table. | And you'll always grumble.
a : I single you out because it's you. | I'm minding it. It's empty. | Somebody has to.

scene em_meal_up_brief
when topic=prices item=meal dir=up
weight 0.6
a : Food's up again. | {price} a meal now. | Another price rise on meals.
b : Again. | Ouch. | Of course there is.
a : Again and again. | I know. | Of course.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Meals cheaper

scene em_meal_down_feast
when topic=prices item=meal dir=down
a : A meal for {price}. I had two. | Cheap food. I'm buying pastries just because. | Supper's cheaper this week. Let's eat out.
b : Two? You'll be round. | Pastries, of course. | Yes. Somewhere with a fire.
a : Round and happy. | Just because. | Somewhere warm.
b?[innkeeper] : Eat up. A full tavern's a happy one.

scene em_meal_down_family
when topic=prices item=meal dir=down band=family|spouses
a : Food's cheaper. Shall we have meat tonight? | The pups ate till they slept. | I bought a whole loaf and didn't count my coin.
b : Meat! Yes. | First quiet night in weeks. | Mark the day.
a : Meat it is. | Let's not wake them. | I did. It's marked.

scene em_meal_down_suspicious
when topic=prices item=meal dir=down
a : Cheap pies. What's in them, I wonder? | {price} for a hot meal. Something's wrong with it. | Never trust cheap stew.
b : Best not to ask. | Or something's right with the harvest. | Never trust a full belly, then.
a : I won't. | We'll see. | I never do.
b?[cook] : Mine is honest meat. Come and smell it yourself.

scene em_meal_down_innkeeper_complains
when topic=prices item=meal dir=down a.job=innkeeper|cook
a : I've lowered my prices and filled every seat and still made less. | Cheaper grain means cheaper suppers means I'm a pauper. | {price} a bowl. I'm feeding the town at cost.
b : Full seats are better than empty ones. | You'll make it up in ale. | Very noble of you.
a : Not if the ale's cheap too. | Ha. That's the plan. | Noble and poor.

scene em_meal_down_children
when topic=prices item=meal dir=down
a : The pups had seconds tonight. | We ate like nobles last night. | For once everyone's fed.
b : Seconds? A good week. | Nobles eat worse, I hear. | For once.
a : A very good week. | Not this week. | Long may it last.

scene em_meal_down_brief
when topic=prices item=meal dir=down
weight 0.6
a : Food's cheaper. | {price} a meal. Better. | Meals are down a little.
b : Good. | Much better. | Little is still something.
a : Very good. | It is. | It is.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Any price

scene em_prices_who_blame
when topic=prices dir=up
weight 0.8
a : Who do we blame this time? | Somebody's getting rich off this. | Prices go up like smoke and come down like stones.
b : The weather. Always the weather. | Never us. | Slowly, and never far enough.
a : Can't fine the weather. | Never us. | Exactly.
b?[official] : The council watches the markets closely.
b?[merchant] : Blame the roads. Every lost cart is a dearer loaf.

scene em_prices_haggle
when topic=prices place=market
a : Watch me haggle. Ten pennies off, I bet. | I got the price down by staring. | Never pay the first price. Never.
b : You'll get two off and a dirty look. | Staring? Teach me. | I always pay the first price.
a : Two's a start. | Ears forward, no blinking. | That's why you're poor.
b?[merchant] : Haggle all you like. My first price is my last.

scene em_prices_saving
when topic=prices band=friends|spouses
a : I've started putting a penny aside every day. | We should buy together and split it. | I keep a jar under the floor for lean weeks.
b : A penny a day? That's a mark by the season. | Good idea. Half the cost. | Under the floor? Don't tell anyone else.
a : That's the plan. | I'll bring the basket. | You're the only one who knows.

scene em_prices_ledger
when topic=prices a.job=official|scholar|merchant
a : I've been writing down prices every week. You'd be surprised. | My ledger says this happens every year about now. | Prices follow the caravans. I can show you.
b : Surprise me. | Every year? | Show me, then.
a : Some other time. It's a long ledger. | Every year. Nobody listens. | Bring a lamp. It's a thick book.

scene em_prices_old_grumble
when topic=prices dir=up a.stage=old
a : I remember when a mark could feed you for a season. | Pennies were worth something in my day. | Every year it costs more to stay alive.
b : Things change. | And now? | And every year you manage.
a : Not always for the better. | Now they're worth less than a smile. | Stubbornness.
b?[child] : What's a mark?

scene em_prices_rumour_cause
when topic=prices dir=up
a : They say a merchant house is buying everything to drive prices up. | I heard the stores were spoiled by damp. | Someone said the price was set by a council in another town.
b : Could be. Merchants are like that. | Damp? Again? | Which council?
a : They're all like that. | Every year. | Nobody ever knows.
